{
  "pdf_page": 411,
  "book_page": 381,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-13",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 3,
      "root": "Qirbah, Qirrâbah",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "Arabic قِرْبَة qirba 'waterskin, leathern bottle' and قَرَّابَة qarrāba 'big jug', both under the Semitic root q-r-b",
      "note": "The root box is right in substance. Arabic قِرْبَة qirba is the ordinary word for a leathern water-bottle/waterskin (Wiktionary places it under the triliteral root ق ر ب, alongside the anatomical 'bladder' and 'bagpipe' senses). The second form Nourai prints, 'Qirrâbah', is the vessel-word that AHD vocalises qarrāba 'big jug' and derives from the II-stem qarraba 'to bring near' (AHD s.v. carboy: 'see qrb in the Appendix of Semitic roots'); Persian lexicography (Dehkhoda, Mo'in) vocalises the borrowed form قَرّابه qarrābe, which points the same way. So Nourai's vowelling 'Qirrâbah' is a harmonisation with qirbah rather than the form the dictionaries print — a vowel choice on an unvocalised skeleton قرابة, not a wrong word, hence no transcription flag. The gloss 'a leathern bottle' fits qirba exactly and qarrāba loosely ('big jug'). Note also the structural point recorded at node #2: on the printed page the arrow to English carboy leaves the PERSIAN box, not the root box.",
      "note_fa": "جعبهٔ ریشه درست است. «قِرْبَة» در عربی مشک یا ظرف چرمیِ آب است و ویکی‌واژه آن را ذیل ریشهٔ سه‌حرفی ق‌-ر-ب می‌آورد. صورت دوم که نورایی «Qirrâbah» ضبط کرده همان واژه‌ای است که فرهنگ American Heritage آن را qarrāba «کوزهٔ بزرگ» می‌خواند و از باب تفعیلِ قَرَّبَ «نزدیک آوردن» می‌گیرد؛ دهخدا و معین نیز صورت فارسیِ وام‌گرفته را «قَرّابه» ضبط کرده‌اند. بنابراین مصوّت‌گذاریِ نورایی (قِرّابه) همسان‌سازی با «قربه» است، نه واژه‌ای نادرست، و چون رسم‌الخط عربیِ «قرابة» بی‌اعراب است، خطای چاپی به شمار نمی‌رود. معنیِ «بطری چرمی» برای قربه کاملاً و برای قرّابه تقریباً درست است.",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.ahdictionary.com/word/search.html?q=carboy",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%D9%82%D8%B1%D8%A8%D8%A9"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {
          "ref": "AHD:202",
          "status": "supports",
          "note": "The 1975/76 New College Edition p.202 (the alphabetical page carrying 'carboy') is not open online, but the AHD etymology is unchanged in the current online edition, ahdictionary.com/word/search.html?q=carboy: '[Persian qarābah, from Arabic qarrāba, big jug, from qarraba, to bring near, derived stem of qaruba, to be near; see qrb in the Appendix of Semitic roots.]' — i.e. exactly Nourai's Arabic root box, with qarrāba where he writes Qirrâbah."
        }
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {
          "src": "KLN",
          "where": "KLN_1966.txt leaf 136 (~p.247-248), s.v. carboy",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "grep -n -i 'carboy' KLN_1966.txt → 'carboy, n., a large glass bottle. — Pers. qaraba. Cp. Arab. qirbah, \"a large leathern bottle\".' Klein's qirbah gloss is word-for-word Nourai's root gloss."
        },
        {
          "src": "HJB",
          "where": "Hobson-Jobson pp. 162b-163a s.v. CARBOY (HJB.txt lines 5240-5263)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'Though it is not an Anglo-Indian word, it comes (in the form ḳarāba) from Persia … Ḳarāba is no doubt connected with Ar. ḳirba, \"a large leathern milk-bottle.\"' Yule cites Kaempfer, Amoen. Exot. 879 (1712) 'quae vocant Karabé' for the Shiraz wine trade."
        },
        {
          "src": "LKT",
          "where": "Lokotsch no. 1074 (LKT.txt line 2549)",
          "stance": "partial",
          "note": "'1074. Pers. ḳārābā: \"Große lederne Milchflasche\" [offenbar mit ar. kirba \"Schlauch\" verwandt]; hieraus engl. carboy' — Lokotsch only says the Persian word is 'evidently related to' Ar. qirba, and does not commit to a direction of borrowing."
        },
        {
          "src": "SKT",
